## SQ-AR-01 | the 9 blueprint recipes with a repeated input list it once, counted (spectral and split arrows, dropper, observer, piston, thunder detector, note block, jukebox)
@group A
@commands `/cdevtest bytype immersiveengineering:blueprint max=400`; `/cdevtest rdetail spectral_arrow`; `/cdevtest rdetail split_arrow`; `/cdevtest rdetail dropper_by_redstonecomponents`; `/cdevtest rdetail observer_by_redstonecomponents`; `/cdevtest rdetail piston_by_redstonecomponents`; `/cdevtest rdetail noteblock`; `/cdevtest rdetail jukebox`; `/cdevtest rdetail thunder`
@pass each of the 9 recipes exists under its old id; in its `ingredients=` list no ingredient appears twice (spectral: glowstone dust once beside the arrow; split: the arrow once beside the wire; dropper and observer: the stone tag once; piston: planks once and stone once; note block and jukebox: planks once; thunder detector: the mundane potion once); no NCH warning in `logs/kubejs/server.log`
@fails `NCH._mergeBlueprintInputs` not called or keyed wrongly (compare `tools/test_nch_blueprint.sh`); an id changed: the id is computed before the merge
> cdevtest bytype immersiveengineering:blueprint max=400
> cdevtest rdetail spectral_arrow
> cdevtest rdetail split_arrow
> cdevtest rdetail dropper_by_redstonecomponents
> cdevtest rdetail observer_by_redstonecomponents
> cdevtest rdetail piston_by_redstonecomponents
> cdevtest rdetail noteblock
> cdevtest rdetail jukebox
> cdevtest rdetail thunder
expect verb=rdetail id=\S*dropper_by_redstonecomponents serializer=immersiveengineering:blueprint
expect verb=rdetail id=\S*observer_by_redstonecomponents serializer=immersiveengineering:blueprint
expect verb=rdetail id=\S*piston_by_redstonecomponents serializer=immersiveengineering:blueprint
kjsreject \[NCH\].*(ieBlueprint|blueprint)
look in every listed blueprint recipe's ingredients= no item list repeats (counts are not printed; a repeated entry is the old form)

## CQ-AR-01 | Engineer's Workbench crafts the arrows with repeated inputs
@group client
@commands survival; Engineer's Workbench with the archery blueprint: 2 glowstone dust + 1 arrow; then 4 arrows + electrum wire; with the redstone components blueprint: 4 stone + quartz + redstone; 3 oak planks + amethyst shard + redstone
@pass 2 spectral arrows; 2 split arrows; an observer; a note block (AR-19); the output slot shows each before taking
@fails the workbench still shows nothing: the merged ingredient lost its count (IE `IngredientWithSize`); a tag ingredient that needs two kinds: the merge did not run for tags
@draft needs a client in a world with an Engineer's Workbench and the blueprints
